# Names koto states deliberately, that tests/doc_names.rs would otherwise
# report. Each record is deferred rather than suppressed.
#
# Format, tab-separated, six fields:
#
#   <kind>  <token>  <category>  <issue>  <witness>  <reason>
#
#   kind       command | path
#   token      the normalized token, e.g. `session rebind` or `docs/foo.md`
#   category   promised    -- a name meant to exist that does not yet
#              intentional -- a name correct as written that will not be built
#   issue      owner/repo#N on a promised record; `-` on an intentional one.
#              A promised record without one is an error. An intentional record
#              WITH one is also an error: a name some issue intends to create is
#              promised, whatever its sentence says about it. That rule is the
#              one half of the category split a machine cannot check, so it is
#              stated here and checked by review.
#   witness    `-` on a promised record. On an intentional one, a digest over
#              the code spans it suppresses, or `?` to have the check print the
#              digest to paste back. Adding an intentional record is therefore
#              deliberately a two-pass operation.
#   reason     free text, required, may contain tabs
#
# A record that stops matching anything is itself a finding, in both
# categories. That is what stops this file rotting into permanent suppression:
# the change that makes a record obsolete is the change that removes it.
#
# The budget is fifteen records and five intentional ones. If you are about to
# exceed either, the thing to question is the finding, not the budget.
#
command	session rebind	promised	tsukumogami/koto#215	-	Specified in docs/designs/current/DESIGN-koto-runs-commands.md as the deliberate re-anchor path and being implemented under that issue. When it lands, this record goes stale AND four passages that state the verb does not exist become false: docs/reference/error-codes.md, plugins/koto-skills/skills/koto-user/SKILL.md, and that skill's error-handling.md and command-reference.md references. Correct all four in the same change that removes this record.
command	migrate	intentional	-	9588e0cd	docs/STABILITY.md commits koto to publishing a migration tool "as `koto migrate` or under a similar discoverable subcommand". The sentence is a forward commitment in a published contract, not a claim that the verb exists today. If a `migrate` subcommand ever ships, this record stops matching and must be removed.
path	.github/workflows/check-templates.yml	intentional	-	0dcb77c1	docs/guides/template-freshness-ci.md tells the reader to add this workflow to THEIR repository; the sentence says "in your repo". It is not a citation of a file in this tree. `.github` is deliberately not an excluded leading segment, because excluding it would blind three live citations of koto's own workflow files to buy this one suppression.
path	docs/diagrams	intentional	-	16f4660c	An output directory in an example workflow configuration in docs/guides/template-freshness-ci.md, created by the job the reader is being shown how to write. A destination, not a citation.
path	docs/my-workflow.html	intentional	-	e552b3d0	The `--output` argument of an example `koto template export` invocation in docs/guides/cli-usage.md. A file the command creates, not one the guide claims exists.
